# Website Repository Workflow

The public website lives in a **separate repository** at `/Users/hamie/Documents/GitHub/hamiebrooklyn.github.io`.

When changes in this bot repo affect the website (new API endpoints, data format changes, new features with a web UI), apply the corresponding frontend changes to the website repo too.

**Before any production deploy or website push:** follow `.cursor/rules/staging-before-production.mdc` — `deploy-mac-staging.sh`, verify on `https://pokepon.org/.../?api=https://api-staging.pokepon.org`, then promote.

When you finish making changes to any file inside that repository (HTML, CSS, JS, images, etc.):

1. **Confirm staging test passed** for this change set.
2. Stage the changed files: `git add` the relevant paths.
3. Commit with a concise message describing the change.
4. **Push (sync) to the remote** on branch **`main`** (GitHub Pages deploys from `main`) — committing alone is not enough:
   `git push origin main`
   If you also maintain `master`, keep it in sync: `git push origin main:master`
4. If commits already exist locally but were not pushed yet, push them before ending the task.
5. After pushing, confirm the live file changed if the user reports stale UI (hard refresh may still be needed for browser cache).

Always commit **and** push automatically at the end of the task — do not wait for the user to ask.
